# Clarity desktop — copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in values.
#   cp .env.example .env.local
#
# You only need TWO files in practice:
#   • `.env.example` — stays in git as documentation (no secrets).
#   • `.env.local` — your real URL + key (gitignored; never commit).
#
# Supabase → Project Settings → API:
#   VITE_SUPABASE_URL     = Project URL (https://xxxxx.supabase.co)
#   VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY = use ONE of the below (same role for this app):
#
#   • **Publishable** key (often `sb_publishable_...`) — use this if the dashboard shows it.
#   • **anon** / **legacy anon** JWT (`eyJ...`) — use this if that’s what your project lists.
#
# Both are public, client-safe keys protected by Row Level Security. Pick whichever
# label Supabase shows for “frontend” / “browser” for your project version.

VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR_PROJECT_REF.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=paste_publishable_or_anon_key_here
